 ## Architecture
 
+### Architecture for non-architects
+
+The system has **three main parts**:
+
+1. **Frontend (React web app)** — applicants and underwriters see a login screen, a document upload form, and a dashboard showing application status. It talks to the backend via simple HTTP requests.
+
+2. **Backend (FastAPI server)** — handles login, stores uploaded documents, kicks off the AI agents to process an application, and lets underwriters manually approve borderline cases. It's the middleman between the web app and the agents.
+
+3. **Agents (LangGraph "brain")** — this is where the magic happens. AI agents read uploaded documents, cross-check facts against registries (Aadhaar/income/property databases), do the lending math, and decide whether to approve/decline the loan. If they're unsure, they flag it for a human.
+
+**Why this design?** We separate concerns so:
+- The web app can be rebuilt without touching the agent logic.
+- The agents can be tested independently with mock documents.
+- Decisions are deterministic where it matters (lending math) and only uses AI where judgment helps (document reading, fact verification).
+
+---
+
