+## Troubleshooting
+
+> **Note:** This section applies to troubleshooting a running deployment. If the system is not yet running (missing backend/frontend code), see the [Setup & installation](#setup--installation) section to complete the initial setup.
+
+### Common errors and solutions
+
+#### "Bedrock model not found" / "model ... is not available"
+**Cause:** The `amazon.nova-pro-v1:0` model is not enabled in your AWS account.
+**Fix:**
+1. Go to the [AWS Bedrock console](https://console.aws.amazon.com/bedrock) → **Model access** (left sidebar)
+2. Click **Manage model access** and enable **Amazon Nova Pro**
+3. Wait a few minutes for activation, then retry
+
+#### "NoCredentialsError" / "Unable to locate credentials"
+**Cause:** AWS credentials are not configured.
+**Fix:**
+```bash
+aws configure  # Enter your access key, secret key, region (us-east-1), output format
+# Or set environment variables:
+export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your_key
+export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your_secret
+export AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1
+```
+
+#### "S3 403 Forbidden" / "Access Denied"
+**Cause:** The S3 bucket exists but your IAM user lacks `s3:GetObject` / `s3:PutObject` permissions.
+**Fix:**
+1. Go to IAM → your user → **Add permissions**
+2. Attach the **AmazonS3FullAccess** policy (or create a custom policy restricting to your bucket)
+
+#### "DynamoDB table not found" / "Requested resource not found"
+**Cause:** The table doesn't exist, or the name in `backend/server.py` is wrong.
+**Fix:**
+1. Go to the [DynamoDB console](https://console.aws.amazon.com/dynamodb)
+2. Create a table with:
+   - **Table name:** matches `DDB_TABLE` in `server.py`
+   - **Partition key:** `application_id` (String)
+   - **Billing:** On-demand (or provisioned 10 RCU / 10 WCU for development)
+3. Wait for the table to be active, then retry
+
+#### "JWT token expired" on every request
+**Cause:** The `JWT_SECRET_KEY` changed between requests (common if using the auto-generated version).
+**Fix:**
+1. Save the `jwt_secret.txt` file (or set `JWT_SECRET_KEY` explicitly in `.env`)
+2. Clear browser cookies and log in again
+
+#### Documents won't upload / "Unsupported file type"
+**Cause:** The document type classification failed, or the document is in an unsupported format.
+**Fix:**
+- Supported formats: **PDF**, **PNG**, **JPG**, **DOCX**
+- Ensure the document matches the slot:
+  - **Identity slot:** Aadhaar or PAN (ID cards)
+  - **Income slot:** Payslip, bank statement, or tax return
+  - **Collateral slot:** Property deed or valuation report
+- Resave the document as PDF if it's been corrupted
+
+#### Application stuck in "processing"
+**Cause:** The background agent job is still running, or crashed without updating the status.
+**Fix:**
+1. Wait 2–5 minutes (agents can take time on first run)
+2. Check the backend logs for errors (in Terminal 1):
+   ```bash
+   # Look for ERROR or exception messages
+   grep -i "error\|exception" <output>
+   ```
+3. If still stuck, check that:
+   - The Bedrock model is enabled
+   - DynamoDB has write permissions
+   - AWS credentials are valid
+
+#### "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'langgraph'"
+**Cause:** Dependencies not installed.
+**Fix:**
+```bash
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+```
 
